*.bak

# Go build output, and the copy apps/vscode/scripts/build-binary.mjs drops into
# apps/vscode/bin/ for packaging -- never commit a built featurelab binary anywhere.
bin/
# `go build ./cmd/featurelab` from the repo root drops the binary HERE, not in bin/, and a 13 MB
# featurelab.exe has already appeared in the root once this way. The ignore is the guard, not the
# habit: git add is not scoped to the paths you name -- it adds to a shared index someone else may
# have staged into -- so an unignored 13 MB artifact is one absent-minded commit away from history
# that cannot be rewritten. No binary is tracked anywhere in this repo, so this masks nothing.
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
/.tmp/

# Node / frontend / apps/vscode build output -- never commit built artifacts,
# packaging fetches or builds them (see frontend/ and apps/vscode/ READMEs).
node_modules/
dist/
out/
*.vsix
*.tsbuildinfo

# apps/desktop (Wails) build output -- `wails build`'s own bin/ output is already covered by
# the bin/ rule above; package.json.md5 is a Wails-internal cache file it drops next to
# frontend/package.json to skip `npm install` when nothing changed.
package.json.md5
.scratch/

# Agent worktrees: `.claude/worktrees/<id>` is a git worktree an assistant session creates to
# work on an isolated copy of this repo. It is scratch by definition -- it holds a second
# checkout, sometimes with deliberately broken code in it -- and must never be committed or
# scanned by repo-wide tooling (a `gofmt -l .` here would report whatever a worktree currently
# has half-written).
.claude/worktrees/

# Working artefacts that keep getting swept up by a repo-wide `git add -A`, twice now.
# Both are REGENERATABLE and neither may ship:
#   apps/vscode/docs/verification/ -- manual UI verification screenshots, taken against whatever
#     pack happened to be open. The committed panel-*.png files beside this directory are the
#     shippable set; screenshots meant to ship are captured against the wiki's own fixture pack
#     (see apps/vscode/scripts/).
#   docs/wiki.zip -- a packaged copy of docs/wiki/, i.e. a second copy of files already in git.
apps/vscode/docs/verification/
docs/wiki.zip

# Python bytecode from ad-hoc analysis scripts run against research/ notes.
__pycache__/

# Stray editor backups. One of these sat in goldentest/ for three weeks.
*.bak
*.orig

# Local working notes -- never tracked, never published.
#
# This directory holds the project's own derivations, its running handoff, and
# the tooling that audits the tree before a release. None of it is part of the
# product and none of it may be published.
#
# Ignoring it rather than deleting it is deliberate: the notes are expensive to
# reproduce, and a tracked copy is one absent-minded `git add -A` from being
# published. Nothing in the build, the tests or CI reads anything under here.
#
# Back it up outside the repo. Git protects none of it: `git clean -xdf` deletes
# the lot.
/research/

# Local-only tests that need an external pack (set via $FEATURELAB_PACK_DIR)
# and a baseline generated from it. They are not part of the repository.
#
# The tracked baseline runs anywhere: goldentest/fixture_test.go against
# docs/wiki/tools/fixtures. goldentest/harness.go reads the pack directory
# from $FEATURELAB_PACK_DIR.
/goldentest/testdata/feature_placement_digest.json
/goldentest/golden_test.go
/goldentest/bench_test.go
/cmd/featurelab/serve_realpack_test.go
/session/profiler_realpack_test.go
